From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Add the layer shell

wlr-layer-shell surfaces (panels, docks, on-screen keyboards) are placed on
their output in four scene layers around the views, background and bottom
below, top and overlay above, and their exclusive zones are kept from the
views, which with one output fill what is left.  Touch and pointer input
reach them as they do views; they take no keyboard focus, so a keyboard
surface types into the application under it.  An output taken away closes
the surfaces on it.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

